>> title: Maamoul
>> category: Cookies
>> tags: semolina, dates, middle eastern, oven, moulded, eid
>> counters: Shawarma Counter
>> aka: maamoul, ma'amoul, mamoul, mamool, maamul, kaak, date maamoul, semolina cookies, date-filled cookies, Eid cookies
>> pairs-with: attar, baklava
>> servings: 24
>> time: 14 hr
>> slack: narrow — eighteen minutes and barely coloured; a maamoul that browns has gone dry and the moulded pattern is lost under the colour

>> step: rub the butter through the semolina
Rub @unsalted butter{1%cup}(225 g; melted and cooled) through @fine semolina{2%cups}(340 g), @coarse semolina{1%cup}(170 g) and @granulated sugar{2%Tbs}(25 g) with your hands until every grain is greased and the mass holds a squeeze.

>> step: rest overnight, 12 hr
Cover @&(~1)buttered semolina{} and ~rest{12%hr} at room temperature.

>> step: knead in the milk and blossom water
Knead @whole milk{1/3%cup}(80 mL), @orange blossom water{2%Tbs}(30 mL), @rose water{1%Tbs}(15 mL), @instant yeast{1/2%tsp} and @mahlab{1/2%tsp}(ground) into @&(~1)rested semolina{} ~knead{2%min} only, until it just comes together and holds a shape.

>> step: work the date paste smooth
Work @pitted dates{2%cups}(340 g; soft Medjool) with @unsalted butter{2%Tbs}(30 g), @ground cinnamon{1/2%tsp} and @ground nutmeg{1/4%tsp} in a #food processor{} to a smooth, pliable paste, then roll it into marble-sized balls.

>> step: mould, fill and seal
Take a walnut of @&(~2)maamoul dough{}, hollow it around your thumb, seat a ball of @&(~1)date paste{} inside, close it over and press it into a wooden #maamoul mould{} to turn it out.

>> step: bake at 350°F 18 min, barely coloured
Bake @&(~1)moulded cookies{} on a lined sheet in the #oven{} at 350°F (175°C) ~bake{18%min}, until the bases are set and the tops still pale. Dust with @powdered sugar{2%Tbs} once cold.
